{
 "_comment": "Starter design system for the Greenshift stylebook. Swap the hex values and font stacks for the brand, keep the structure. Prefix `gt-` can be renamed per project — if you rename it, rename it in the layout classes too. Text tokens (--gt-ink, --gt-muted, --gt-purple, --gt-olive-text, --gt-accent-text) pass WCAG AA (4.5:1) against the surface tokens. --gt-olive and --gt-accent are decorative fills that FAIL as body text on a light surface, which is exactly why the -text variants exist — use those for type. Re-run scripts/check_contrast.py after changing any value. Each variable carries a `kind` (color, font-size, spacing, font-family, custom); `stylebook.py push --theme` uses it to register the token as a theme.json preset and alias the gt- name onto it, and an optional `alias` names an existing theme variable to point at instead.",
